KHYRAT LEGAL CONTENT ENGINE — FULL PROJECT CONTEXT
Updated: 2026-10-21 (Africa/Cairo)
Repository: https://github.com/mr-romel/khyrat-legal-content-engine
Production branch: main
Primary purpose: automate verified Egyptian legal content, platform-specific drafting, image generation and QA, scheduled publishing, engagement, Reels, Telegram review, Blogger SEO/search-demand publishing, and marketplace workflows.

IMPORTANT TRUTH RULE
Never claim success because a commit exists, a workflow is green, a sheet cell changed, or a UI modal closed. For external actions require a public permalink, remote platform post/video ID, Telegram message receipt/ID, or Blogger public permalink. Always distinguish implemented code, test pass, workflow completion, and externally verified publication.

PROJECT MISSION AND NON-NEGOTIABLE RULES
- Produce useful, accurate Egyptian legal content in natural professional Egyptian Arabic.
- Verify current Egyptian law, amendments, dates and official source URLs. Never invent article/statute numbers, penalties, deadlines, case numbers, court principles, quotations or citations.
- Avoid robotic filler, repeated generic hooks, AI-production disclosures, internal labels, ellipses, incomplete endings and hard-sell CTA.
- Do not publish the same Facebook caption on LinkedIn. Facts may overlap, copy and audience framing must not.
- Reuse a topic only with a materially different angle, purpose, hook, examples or practical treatment.
- Exactly one intended slot per calendar day, Africa/Cairo, deterministic but variable from 10:00 to 22:00 inclusive. No even/odd-date filter.
- Retries must be idempotent. Persist destination IDs/URLs immediately and retry only the failed destination after partial success.
- Never commit or log API keys, tokens, OAuth JSON, service-account JSON, cookies or browser storage state. Document secret names only.
- Do not assume ungranted API scopes. LinkedIn scope previously confirmed: w_member_social; do not assume w_member_social_feed.
- Provider free tiers and quota are not guaranteed. Gemini 429 can be project-level; stop cycling model names and use a verified-source fallback where safe.
- Never bulk-delete Blogger drafts without checking IDs, titles, body and state.

CURRENT TOP PRIORITIES
1. Latest Quality Check failed at tests/test_reel_overlay_duration_cap.py. Compile and imports passed, AI router tests passed; a targeted Reel test group failed and later test groups were skipped. Run: https://github.com/mr-romel/khyrat-legal-content-engine/actions/runs/39656731747
2. Failure appears to be a stale assertion: test expects two legacy FFmpeg command strings, but src/reel_pipeline.py now removes the duplicate whiteboard/card layer, sets styled = base, concatenates base plus end card, then burns subtitles separately. Update the test to verify the current architecture; do not delete the regression test.
3. src/image_qa.py currently returns decision PASS and scores 100 when QA key is missing or the vision API throws. This is misleading: QA was not performed. Replace with explicit PASS / REGENERATE / QA_SKIPPED / QA_ERROR states; if visual QA is unavailable, permit text-only publishing only when policy allows and do not attach an unverified image.
4. Blogger REST OAuth previously returned invalid_grant. If persistent, owner must reauthorize Blogger scope and replace BLOGGER_OAUTH_JSON securely. Code cannot revive a revoked refresh token.
5. Reel single subtitle-box change needs actual MP4 inspection and a current successful production run. Check vertical dimensions, duration, sound, one box, full sentence, no clipping, end card, Telegram message ID and Shorts URL/ID if enabled.
6. LinkedIn image-repair copy path changed in commit 606223916b2b2900c49c7805b80694679dbac8ed; test normal and repair paths, including generation fallback, then inspect actual LinkedIn post ID/text.

ARCHITECTURE / FILE RESPONSIBILITIES
Main pipeline:
- src/run_main.py: production entry/runner.
- src/main.py: coordinates topic selection, drafting, editorial prep, image, Facebook/LinkedIn publication, state and notifications.
- src/content_system.py and src/content_system_runtime.py: content strategy/runtime.
- src/content_planner.py, src/social_content.py, src/content_style.py, src/content_style_v3.py: planning, sanitization, platform copy and style.
- src/post_bank.py: history and prior-content context.
- src/topic_bank.py, src/topic_bank_500.py, src/topic_bank_expanded.py: subject pools.
- src/daily_schedule.py: one stable variable slot/day.
- src/monthly_recycler.py, src/recycler_rules.py: topic rotation, angle selection and canonical keys.
- src/decision_engine.py, src/content_diversity.py, src/content_similarity.py, src/editorial_review.py: selection and quality gates.
- src/analytics.py, src/performance.py, src/production_monitor.py: logs, metrics and monitoring.

AI and legal research:
- src/gemini.py, src/gemini_runtime.py, src/gemini_chat.py: generation.
- src/ai_router.py: provider/model routing and fallback.
- src/legal_research.py and src/legal_reference_registry.py: legal-source research/reference records.
- src/search_console_intelligence.py and src/search_geo.py: search-demand and SEO/GEO metadata.
- Specific legal claims must be traceable to official/current source URLs; a generated citation is not source verification.

Images:
- src/image_generator.py: provider integration, post-derived visual brief, output and brand overlay.
- src/image_qa.py: final-image QA.
- src/free_media.py: media fallback.
- Preserve .provenance.json containing provider/model, exact prompt, prompt hash, final image hash and QA status.
- Debug the actual final image: post -> brief -> provider/model -> file -> provenance -> QA -> uploaded asset.
- Contemporary legal topics must not receive irrelevant ancient/Pharaonic visuals.
- Current image QA behavior is unsafe/misleading for status: missing key/API errors are returned as PASS with scores 100. Correct the state model before calling QA reliable.
- The existing prompt imposes a project policy of no women or girls in generated images; this is a project-specific constraint.

Reels and video:
- src/reel_pipeline.py: narration, video assembly, brand end card, subtitle integration, final validation and Telegram handoff.
- src/reel_subtitles.py: timed Arabic sentence captions in one adaptive box.
- src/reel_publishers.py, src/video_layer.py, src/video_module/*: publishing and modular video logic.
- src/telegram_publication.py, src/telegram_bot.py, src/telegram_control.py: delivery/review/approval.
- Required behavior: vertical 9:16; one subtitle box visible at a time; all spoken sentence text fits inside frame; no duplicate layer, clipping, missing words or broken Arabic shaping; one brand end card; final duration within configured bounds.
- Use actual TTS segment timing. Bound looped FFmpeg inputs and verify final MP4 rather than relying on source tests only.
- If YouTube Shorts is enabled, use the related post text as description and store actual video URL/ID.

Social and engagement:
- src/facebook_publisher.py and src/linkedin_publisher.py: platform publishers.
- src/facebook_engagement_worker.py, src/facebook_private_reply_worker.py, src/linkedin_engagement.py, src/linkedin_engagement_worker.py, src/linkedin_comment_engine.py: engagement.
- src/comment_engine.py and src/engagement_strategy.py: comment generation/strategy.
- Intended variable queue: 3–7 contextual comments per post/platform. Worker publishes at most one pending comment/run where configured and must be idempotent. Optional reaction/comment failure must not undo a successful base post.
- LinkedIn is B2B legal/business copy for owners, management, HR, legal, compliance and operations; roughly 350–600 Arabic words when topic supports it; target business impact, operational risk, documents, responsibility and decisions. Avoid direct “أنت/إنت/عندك” address and sales pitch. Keep within 2,900 characters. Distinct copy on every path including image repair.

Blogger:
- src/blogger_worker.py: planned article publishing.
- src/blogger_demand_worker.py: demand research and extra article.
- src/blogger_publisher.py: REST/OAuth/HTML/labels.
- src/blogger_ui_publisher.py: Playwright fallback and permalink verification.
- src/blogger_editor.py, src/blogger_seo_worker.py, src/blogger_intelligence.py, src/blogger_identity_worker.py, src/blogger_pages.py, src/blogger_pages_ui_worker.py, src/blogger_site_setup.py: supporting SEO/site tasks.
- Verified article: https://askmahmoudkhyrat.blogspot.com/2026/10/blog-post_314.html
  Title: كيفية التعامل مع الابتزاز الإلكتروني في مصر: الأدلة والخطوات القانونية التي يجب مراجعتها
- REST OAuth invalid_grant requires owner reauthorization if persistent; update BLOGGER_OAUTH_JSON through secret management, never chat.
- Gemini 429: stop cycling model names; use conservative source-grounded fallback.
- Normalize combined labels below Blogger's limit. On retry reuse exact existing published article. Do not bulk-delete drafts.
- UI success means exact title in Published state plus public permalink, not modal closure.

State/config:
