KNOWN ISSUES AND SOLUTIONS
P0 Quality Check:
- Evidence: run 39656731747 failed at test_both_whiteboard_overlay_paths_are_duration_bounded. Compile/import and AI router tests passed; downstream test groups skipped.
- Cause: stale test searches for old exact FFmpeg string twice, but implementation now uses a single base video and separate subtitle burn.
- Solution: update test to assert current architecture: duplicate overlay absent, base + end card concatenated once, subtitle burn used once, final duration validated; then rerun focused tests and full Quality Check.

P0 Image QA truthfulness:
- Cause: fail-open was represented as PASS/100 when QA did not run.
- Solution: explicit QA_SKIPPED / QA_ERROR; never synthesize scores. If unavailable, text-only fallback may proceed according to policy but image must not be presented as inspected.

P0 Blogger OAuth:
- Cause: expired/revoked refresh token or OAuth client setup.
- Solution: account owner reauthorizes with correct Blogger scope, updates BLOGGER_OAUTH_JSON securely, then checks OAuth health. Application code cannot repair revoked credentials.

P1 Reel verification:
- Earlier row 23 successfully rendered at 69.8 seconds and Telegram delivery was logged in run 38055595685.
- New single-box architecture still requires latest actual MP4 inspection and Telegram receipt.
- Verify dimensions, duration, narration, caption overflow, no duplicate box, end card, Telegram ID and Shorts URL if enabled.

P1 LinkedIn:
- Commit 606223916b2b2900c49c7805b80694679dbac8ed updated image-repair path to create LinkedIn-specific copy.
- Test regular and image-repair paths, fallback behavior and cross-platform similarity; verify actual LinkedIn post ID/text.

P1 retries:
- Per-platform partial success can create duplicates if retry republishes all destinations.
- Persist platform-specific idempotency key, remote ID/URL and status; retry only missing destinations.

P1 observability:
- Standardize events: run ID, content row/key, platform, action, status, remote ID/URL, retry count, error class, QA state, timestamp. Redact credentials. Daily report must separate workflow completion from external proof.

P2 legal/content diversity:
- Track source URLs, retrieval dates, angle and content fingerprint. Semantic similarity should prompt review, not replace legal-source verification.

P2 provider failures:
- Classify quota/auth/transient/invalid-response/hard failures. Retry only transient errors with bounded exponential backoff. Stop on auth errors; use verified-source fallback for quota errors.

